Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of the Special Committee on Agriculture, Fisheries and Rural Communities

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on the Establishment and Operation of the Special Committee on Agriculture, Fisheries and Rural Communities, and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.

Article 2 (Preparation and Management of Minutes) The Special Committee on Agriculture, Fisheries and Rural Communities established under Article 2 (1) of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of the Special Committee on Agriculture, Fisheries and Rural Communities (hereinafter referred to as the "Act" and the "Committee", respectively) shall record the following matters in the minutes of its meetings and manage and preserve such minutes pursuant to the Public Records Management Act:
1. The date, time, and place of the meeting, and whether it was open to the public;
2. A list of members in attendance;
3. Details of agenda items submitted and the results of consultations;
4. Other major matters discussed.

Article 3 (Establishment and Composition of Subcommittees)
(1) Subcommittees established under Article 8 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "subcommittees") shall be classified and established as the Agricultural Subcommittee, Fisheries Subcommittee, Forestry Subcommittee, Rural Communities Subcommittee, and Agricultural and Fisheries Food Subcommittee. <Amended on June 2, 2025>
(2) Each subcommittee shall consist of no more than 20 members, including one chairperson of the subcommittee (hereinafter referred to as a "subcommittee chairperson").

Article 4 (Jurisdiction and Duties of Subcommittees)
(1) Matters under the jurisdiction of each subcommittee shall be as follows: <Amended on June 2, 2025>
1. Agricultural Subcommittee: The following matters:
  (a) Medium- and long-term policy directions for the sustainable development of agriculture (excluding forestry; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph) and realization of its public-interest functions;
  (b) Establishment of autonomous agricultural policies based on local autonomy and decentralization;
  (c) Inter-Korean cooperation in agriculture;
  (d) Realization of the multiple values of agriculture;
2. Fisheries Subcommittee: The following matters:
  (a) Medium- and long-term policy directions for the sustainable development of the fisheries industry (limited to fishing and aquaculture; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph) and realization of its public-interest functions;
  (b) Establishment of autonomous fisheries policies based on local autonomy and decentralization;
  (c) Inter-Korean cooperation in the fisheries industry;
  (d) Realization of the multiple values of the fisheries industry;
3. Forestry Subcommittee: The following matters:
  (a) Medium- and long-term policy directions for the sustainable development of forestry and realization of its public-interest functions;
  (b) Establishment of autonomous forestry policies based on local autonomy and decentralization;
  (c) Inter-Korean cooperation in forestry;
  (d) Realization of the multiple values of forestry;
4. Rural Communities Subcommittee: The following matters:
  (a) Medium- and long-term policy directions for the sustainable development of rural communities and realization of their public-interest functions;
  (b) Realization of the multiple values of rural communities;
  (c) Regional development and enhancement of welfare in rural communities;
  (d) Systematic preservation and efficient utilization of rural ecosystems, environments, and resources;
5. Agricultural and Fisheries Food Subcommittee: The following matters:
  (a) Matters concerning all aspects of food, including production, processing, supply, and consumption of agricultural and fisheries products;
  (b) Matters concerning research and development in the agricultural and fisheries food sector.
(2) Each subcommittee shall perform the following duties concerning matters under its jurisdiction and report the results to the Committee:
1. Review and coordination of agenda items to be submitted to the Committee;
2. Collection of public opinions and domestic and international investigation and research, including surveys, public hearings, and seminars, for the performance of the Committee's duties;
3. Handling other matters delegated by the Committee.

Article 5 (Operation of Subcommittees)
(1) A subcommittee meeting shall be convened in any of the following cases:
1. Where the chairperson of the Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "chairperson") or at least five Committee members request a meeting;
2. Where at least one third of the incumbent members of the subcommittee request a meeting;
3. Where the subcommittee chairperson otherwise deems a meeting necessary.
(2) The subcommittee chairperson shall convene and preside over meetings of the subcommittee.
(3) A subcommittee meeting shall open with the attendance of a majority of its incumbent members and shall adopt resolutions with the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(4) Where necessary to perform duties, the subcommittee chairperson may request relevant administrative officials, officers or employees of producer organizations, farmers or fishers, or other experts to attend a subcommittee meeting and state their opinions.
(5) Article 2 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the preparation of minutes of subcommittee meetings. In such cases, "Committee" shall be construed as "subcommittee", "members" as "subcommittee members", and "results of consultations" as "results of review and coordination".

Article 6 (Composition, etc. of Special Committees)
(1) A special committee established under Article 8 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "special committee") shall consist of no more than 15 members, including its chairperson (hereinafter referred to as a "special committee chairperson").
(2) A special committee chairperson shall be designated by the chairperson of the Committee from among Committee members, or commissioned by the chairperson from among experts in fields related to agriculture, fisheries, and rural communities.
(3) Members of a special committee shall be commissioned by the chairperson, after hearing the special committee chairperson's opinion, from among experts with extensive knowledge and experience concerning specific pending issues related to agriculture, fisheries, and rural communities.
(4) The existence of a special committee shall be limited to a maximum of one year: Provided, That where necessary, the period may be extended once only, by no more than one year, following a resolution of the Committee.

Article 7 (Operation of the Secretariat) The head of the secretariat established under the Committee pursuant to Article 9 (1) of the Act shall be a person designated by the chairperson upon the recommendation of the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, after the Minister has heard the opinion of the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries. <Amended on May 9, 2023>

Article 8 (Allowances, etc.) Allowances, travel expenses, and other necessary expenses may be paid, within the budget, to members, experts, and others attending meetings of the Committee, subcommittees, and special committees: Provided, That payments shall not be made to public officials attending in direct connection with their assigned duties.

Article 9 (Detailed Rules of Operation) Matters necessary for the operation of the Committee, subcommittees, and special committees, other than those prescribed in this Decree, shall be determined by the chairperson following a resolution of the Committee.

ADDENDA <No. 29712, April 25, 2019>

This Decree shall enter into force on April 25, 2019.

ADDENDA <No. 33453, May 9, 2023>

This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.

ADDENDA <No. 35584, June 2, 2025>

This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
